---
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';
import SiteLink from '../components/SiteLink.astro';
import {
  APP_NAME,
  BUSINESS_NAME,
  SUPPORT_EMAIL,
} from 'astro:env/client';

const effectiveDate = 'April 20, 2026';
---

<Doc
  title={`Privacy | ${APP_NAME}`}
  description={`How ${APP_NAME} handles data. Anonymous analytics via TelemetryDeck, nothing else.`}
>
  <header class="doc__header">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="doc__meta">Effective: {effectiveDate}.</p>
  </header>

  <p>
    Short version: we can't see your drawings. {APP_NAME} has no
    server of its own. Your drawings and game state travel inside the
    iMessage URL, directly from your phone to your friend's, and we
    never touch them. Apple handles any in-app purchases. The only
    thing that reaches us is the anonymous app analytics described
    below.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>
      We use TelemetryDeck for anonymous usage analytics. Under GDPR,
      our basis is Art. 6(1)(f) legitimate interest: we need a reliable
      way to understand how the app gets used.
    </p>
    <p>Data transferred:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>An anonymized, untraceable user ID (per app installation).</li>
      <li>Actions defined by the app publisher (for example, "app launched," "settings opened").</li>
      <li>Rounded timestamps (nearest hour).</li>
      <li>Device metadata (system and app version, device type).</li>
      <li>Publisher-defined metadata.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Data not collected:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>No IP addresses (not in logs, not in the database).</li>
      <li>No cookies or tracking technologies.</li>
      <li>No persistent identifiers that could be traced back to individuals.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How we use it</h2>
    <p>
      We look at this data to see which features get used, find bugs,
      and make the app better. That's the list. No ads, no user
      profiles, no selling.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Drawings and reports</h2>
    <p>
      Your drawings go directly to the people you send them to, through
      iMessage. We're not in the middle. If a word the app gave you
      looks wrong or offensive, tap Report on it and an email lands
      with us. We'll have a look. To stop hearing from a specific
      player, use iMessage's block feature.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Payments</h2>
    <p>
      We never see your payment info. Apple handles any in-app
      purchases under <SiteLink
        href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/"
        target="_blank"
        aria-label="Apple's privacy policy, opens in new tab"
      >Apple's privacy policy</SiteLink>&#8288;.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Who handles the analytics</h2>
    <p>
      TelemetryDeck GmbH runs the analytics, out of Germany
      (Von-der-Tann-Str. 54, 86159 Augsburg). Their privacy policy is
      at <SiteLink
        href="https://telemetrydeck.com/privacy"
        target="_blank"
        aria-label="TelemetryDeck privacy policy, opens in new tab"
      >telemetrydeck.com/privacy</SiteLink>&#8288;. They're held to the
      same standard this page describes.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Keeping and deleting data</h2>
    <p>
      The analytics data is anonymous, so there's no personal record of
      you sitting around to keep or delete. If you want it off
      entirely, the app has an Analytics toggle. After you turn it off,
      nothing else gets sent.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Your GDPR rights</h2>
    <p>
      Under GDPR, you have the right to access, correct, or object to
      the processing of personal data that relates to you. The catch
      with this app: the analytics above can't be traced back to a
      person, so there usually isn't a record tied to you. If we can't
      find one, we'll say so.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Do Not Track</h2>
    <p>This app does not track your online activities across third-party websites or services.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>
      {APP_NAME} isn't aimed at kids under 13, and we don't knowingly
      collect info from them.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>If this page changes</h2>
    <p>
      When something important here changes, we'll bump the effective
      date up top and show a notice in the app before it takes effect.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Questions?</h2>
    <p>
      Email <SiteLink href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</SiteLink>&#8288;.
      {BUSINESS_NAME} runs the app and maintains this page.
    </p>
  </section>
</Doc>
